; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Spiral Explorer
; CATEGORY: Spirals & Curves
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     input, readlist, polyspi, angles, experiment
; SUMMARY:  Asks you for an angle and draws the spiral that angle makes, so you can hunt for beautiful angles.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   You type an angle. The turtle draws a spiral by walking, turning
;   that angle, and walking a little further each time. Then it asks
;   for another angle. Some angles give squares, some stars, some
;   flowers, and some angles just a little different from those give
;   twisting spirals.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Type an angle from 1 to 359 in the command center and
;   press Enter. Type quit to stop. Good ones to try: 90, 89, 121,
;   144, 145, 170, 59, 72, 100, 135.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * READLIST and checking the answer before using it
;   * an angle close to 360 / n gives a twisting n-sided spiral
;   * the same small procedure can draw hundreds of different pictures
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Find an angle that makes a spiral with 5 arms.
;   * Ask for the step growth as well as the angle.
;   * Keep a list of the angles the user liked, and print it at the end.
; ============================================================

; One spiral: walk, turn, walk a bit further. Stop when the steps
; would carry the turtle off the screen.
to spiral :angle
  localmake "step 2
  localmake "hue 0
  while [:step < 300] [
    setpencolor (list 128 + 120 * sin :hue 128 + 120 * sin :hue + 120 128 + 120 * sin :hue + 240)
    forward :step
    right :angle
    make "step :step + 1.5
    make "hue :hue + 3
  ]
end

; Ask for an angle until we get a sensible one. Outputs the angle,
; or the word quit.
to askangle
  print [Type an angle from 1 to 359, or quit:]
  localmake "answer readlist
  if emptyp :answer [output askangle]
  localmake "a first :answer
  if equalp lowercase :a "quit [output "quit]
  if not numberp :a [print [That is not a number.] output askangle]
  if or :a < 1 :a > 359 [print [Please choose between 1 and 359.] output askangle]
  output :a
end

to explore
  forever [
    localmake "angle askangle
    if equalp :angle "quit [print [Happy spiraling!] stop]
    clean
    penup home pendown
    spiral :angle
    penup setxy -390 -290 setpencolor [200 200 200]
    label (sentence [angle] :angle)
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [20 20 30]
setpensize 2
explore
